# Browser safety rules Netlify sends with every page (Netlify reads this file from the build output).
# Content-Security-Policy: only our own scripts run (no inline code, nothing injected); styles may be inline (Angular adds them);
#   fonts from Google Fonts; images from us, data: pictures and https sites (uploaded photos); calls only to our own address.
#   At the deploy, if the API is on another address, add it to connect-src (backend/PLAN.md › The deploy).
# X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors: no other site may show these pages inside a frame (clickjacking).
# The rest: files keep their type, addresses aren't leaked to other sites, no camera/mic/location, always HTTPS.
# A staff panel: keep it out of search results too.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
